#: ../../source/docs/common-mamba-basic-mk3.rst:68
#: 234f2c1189a14cc89de9c13265db2c84
msgid "The PPM pin, which by default is mapped to a timer input, can be used for all ArduPilot supported receiver protocols, except CRSF/ELRS and SRXL2 which require a true UART connection. However, FPort, when connected in this manner, will only provide RC without telemetry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mamba-basic-mk3.rst:70
#: 166b768ca7524928ad6b044a8a652704
msgid "To allow CRSF and embedded telemetry available in Fport, CRSF, and SRXL2 receivers, the SBUS pin can also be configured to be used as true UART1 RX pin for use with bi-directional systems by setting the :ref:`BRD_ALT_CONFIG<BRD_ALT_CONFIG>` to “1” so it becomes the SERIAL1 port's RX input pin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mamba-basic-mk3.rst:72
#: 5b43c461e20d4851845f08eba992cd6c
msgid "With this option, :ref:`SERIAL1_PROTOCOL<SERIAL1_PROTOCOL>` must be set to \"23\", and:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mamba-basic-mk3.rst:74
#: 2c00f55b34814157884d76fec44fa96e
msgid "PPM is not supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mamba-basic-mk3.rst:76
#: bd2694910bfa406789b6ce6aba6b8404
msgid "SBUS/DSM/SRXL connects to the PPM pin, but SBUS is not supported without an external inverter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mamba-basic-mk3.rst:78
#: c8423ca64ada4126900e3b8359c0c974
msgid "FPort requires connection to T1 and PPM(R1) via a bi-directional inverter. See :ref:`common-FPort-receivers`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mamba-basic-mk3.rst:80
#: 15781b4fc2214fd988e569071d3f04e4
msgid "CRSF also requires a T1 connection, in addition to PPM (R1), and automatically provides telemetry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mamba-basic-mk3.rst:82
#: a042090cf1b143a0bf124676de83c788
msgid "SRXL2 requires a connection to T1 and automatically provides telemetry.  Set :ref:`SERIAL1_OPTIONS<SERIAL1_OPTIONS>` to \"4\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mamba-basic-mk3.rst:84
#: 2a47b9591309487e91e4619778d7f6c8
msgid "Any UART can be used for RC system connections in ArduPilot also, and is compatible with all protocols except PPM (SBUS requires external inversion). See :ref:`common-rc-systems` for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mamba-basic-mk3.rst:88
#: 32666e7e4cfa4fa39c8335756cbb8a4a
msgid "OSD Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mamba-basic-mk3.rst:90
#: e38e3eed3aa44fab89274137ed88a785
msgid "The Mamba F405 MK2 has an integrated OSD enabled by :ref:`OSD_TYPE<OSD_TYPE>` =` 1 (MAX7456 driver)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mamba-basic-mk3.rst:93
#: de256be8dce843daa6a9540aa6ada440
msgid "PWM Output"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mamba-basic-mk3.rst:95
#: 8d2b42033e604a25aad8c11677d55e05
msgid "The Mamba F405 MK2 supports up to 4 PWM outputs. The pads for motor output ESC1 to ESC4 on the above diagram are for the 4 outputs. All 4 outputs support DShot as well as all PWM types."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mamba-basic-mk3.rst:97
#: 849e55671b0149e591b3130f488c7ed3
msgid "The outputs are all in one group."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mamba-basic-mk3.rst:99
#: d2a03ab29a034c0ea6ad55bb39228c12
msgid "Channels within the same group need to use the same output rate. If any channel in a group uses DShot then all channels in the group need to use DShot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mamba-basic-mk3.rst:104
#: 7241a94809d84957a20b7dd6431c638f
msgid "Battery Monitoring"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mamba-basic-mk3.rst:106
#: ed5f7cc2072a4c0ea709608735386bec
msgid "The board has a built-in voltage sensor. The voltage sensor can handle up to 6S LiPo batteries. An external current sense input is also provided."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mamba-basic-mk3.rst:109
#: c87876a099b7464caafa0e8012f41bdb
msgid "The correct battery setting parameters are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mamba-basic-mk3.rst:111
#: 2c74fba32d6c4072823cccb923bbdd3c
msgid ":ref:`BATT_MONITOR<BATT_MONITOR>` = 3 for voltage only or = 4 if external current sense is also used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mamba-basic-mk3.rst:112
#: 34dd7a49c30e4c91a129a103f5e341c4
msgid ":ref:`BATT_VOLT_PIN<BATT_VOLT_PIN__AP_BattMonitor_Analog>` = 11"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mamba-basic-mk3.rst:113
#: 97326e1ba28949509b8a9278fc30a209
msgid ":ref:`BATT_VOLT_MULT<BATT_VOLT_MULT__AP_BattMonitor_Analog>` = 11.0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mamba-basic-mk3.rst:114
#: 1e6f6cedaef84836a7fb447d93152f22
msgid ":ref:`BATT_CURR_PIN<BATT_CURR_PIN__AP_BattMonitor_Analog>` = 13"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mamba-basic-mk3.rst:115
#: 89a12dc2ae24431da53aa992ea07d63f
msgid ":ref:`BATT_AMP_PERVLT<BATT_AMP_PERVLT__AP_BattMonitor_Analog>` depends on external current sensor used"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mamba-basic-mk3.rst:118
#: a3e9f5cf77934d90a92828be38cd4d7c
msgid "Compass"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mamba-basic-mk3.rst:120
#: 07719c7c893945c588e3aa52b4880e43
msgid "The Mamba Basic autopilots do not have a builtin compass, but you can attach an external compass using I2C on the SDA and SCL pads or refer to :ref:`common-compassless`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mamba-basic-mk3.rst:123
#: 6932bb09cb9f4b94a60f0f53d5e9a246
msgid "Firmware"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mamba-basic-mk3.rst:125
#: 1835c6ad7c9f4bfe9f8c1ab63543765f
msgid "Firmware for this board can be found `here <https://firmware.ardupilot.org>`__ in  sub-folders labeled \"MambaF405US-I2C\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mamba-basic-mk3.rst:127
#: 759f7fd3b03a42a1823725264d17242e
msgid "Initial firmware load can be done with DFU by plugging in USB with the bootloader button pressed. Then you should load the \"with_bl.hex\" firmware. See :ref:`common-loading-firmware-onto-chibios-only-boards`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mamba-basic-mk3.rst:131
#: bf4a46e7631b4931ba007bcec96c9885
msgid "Once the initial firmware is loaded you can update the firmware using any ArduPilot ground station software. Updates should be done with the \".apj\" firmware files."
msgstr ""
